 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? That's a big step into the big world. Do you want something big and expensive, like theme park, or something cheaper but just as fun, like zoo or castle tour? Zoo would give him new animals to stare at, and sometimes they have shows. Castle is history and adventure without wearying him. Zoo ticket prices come down quite a bit after the busy summer months. Check with the local authority if he gets a discount. Then stick to the menu and keep an eye on time so he doesn't get stuck there. Some little ones get upset when their friend leaves. Zoo usually need them, so ask at the gate. Castles often offer room for a quick lunch, so check first there too.",
